  "notes": [
    [
      "One run, two franchises.",
      "The lines are interleaved exactly as they came out, because that is the order the rumour grew in. The chips at the top hide a whole line — Alien, Predator, or the crossovers — so either franchise can be watched on its own. Hiding a line redraws the bar; it never unticks anything."
    ],
    [
      "Sections are eras, not decades.",
      "The shared twentieth century, the two crossovers, the 2010s returns, and the Disney years. The crossovers get their own heading because they are the reason these two series share a page."
    ],
    [
      "Weights are runtimes.",
      "A film's width in the bar is its length in hours. Alien: Earth is one row for the whole season, 8 episodes counted at the midpoint of the 45–64-minute range its own infobox gives."
    ],
    [
      "What is not here.",
      "Predator: Killer of Killers, the animated anthology — this list is the theatrical run, plus Prey and the television series. The two Alien vs. Predator films stay, marked Crossover, because they came out in the middle of it."
